 What Drey may do                                                      Esc back

  Drey is the dock on your desktop. Each bar says how much Drey may do on
  its own for one kind of action; everything else it can only show you. Less
  is to the left. Drey can lower a bar itself, never raise one. Saying no,
  pausing and stopping are always allowed from Drey.


▎ Everyday answers        █ █ █ █ ·   Answer in your words
    Also answer an agent in your own words, shown whole in Drey's confirm
    window; never to an agent holding desktop control.

  Stop and close          █ ░ · · ·   What Den can undo
    Close an agent; you can reopen it.

  Run commands            █ · · · ·   One command, shown whole
    Run one command from Drey's confirm window, once, never 'always'.

  Desktop control         ░ ░ · · ·   Only in Den
    Drey shows it; you act in Den's window.

  Send out                ░ ░ ░ · ·   Only in Den
    Drey shows it; you act in Den's window.

  Saying no, pausing and stopping are always allowed from Drey.
  Raising permissions, "always allow" and pairing are done in Den.

  DEN ONLY
    Turn on God mode
    Pair or re-pair a console, add a console
    Turn the API on or unlock it
    Raise any level here
    Turn off or loosen a check (rate limits, read-first, input idle, desktop
    pause, the audit)
    Anything about a remote host
    Widen permissions: "always", raising the mode, installs, allowing a
    refused click, reading private files
    Keep going over a budget, resume or set the weekly usage limit
    Den's own window, ending your session, reloading Hyprland, the panic key